279
00:20:43.522 --> 00:20:46.210
Grocery Schema and Data Evolution Standard.

280
00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:48.207
Note:

281
00:20:48.487 --> 00:20:53.735
Design Document (excerpt), Schema and Data Evolution Standard v1.2.

282
00:20:54.015 --> 00:20:54.911
Status:

283
00:20:55.191 --> 00:20:56.471
Accepted, Authors:

284
00:20:56.751 --> 00:20:58.543
Platform Data Guild, Reviewers:

285
00:20:58.823 --> 00:21:01.233
DBA, SRE, Service leads.

286
00:21:01.513 --> 00:21:15.295
Context, 26 services, several sharing databases; a 40M-row orders table; a Kafka event bus with independently-deployed consumers; mobile + partner API clients that upgrade slowly.

287
00:21:15.575 --> 00:21:18.369
A past in-place ALTER caused a 9-minute outage.

288
00:21:18.649 --> 00:21:28.591
Decision, All schema, message, and API changes MUST be expand or contract and MUST keep every intermediate state backward- and forward-compatible.

289
00:21:28.871 --> 00:21:32.988
Destructive steps are separate, last, and gated on usage telemetry.

290
00:21:34.338 --> 00:22:03.601
Related ADRs, ADR-140 Online-DDL rules (metadata-only or CONCURRENTLY or NOT VALID+VALIDATE); ADR-141 Expand or contract for all column changes; ADR-142 Batched backfills only; ADR-143 Protobuf on the bus under FULL compatibility in a registry; ADR-144 API additive-first, /vN only for breaks,

291
00:22:03.881 --> 00:22:16.339
Sunset headers; ADR-145 Store-to-store migration via dual-write+reconcile; ADR-146 Forward-only versioned migrations in the pipeline.

292
00:22:16.619 --> 00:22:17.579
Requirements.

293
00:22:17.859 --> 00:22:19.289
R1, No outage.

294
00:22:19.569 --> 00:22:26.331
No migration may hold ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on a large table for more than the locktimeout (3 s in prod).

295
00:22:26.611 --> 00:22:28.809
Table rewrites under lock are forbidden.

296
00:22:30.159 --> 00:22:31.567
R2, Rolling-safe.

297
00:22:31.847 --> 00:22:40.572
Every migration must be compatible with the currently-deployed code AND the code being rolled out (both directions), so a rollback at any step is safe.

298
00:22:40.852 --> 00:22:42.303
R3, Bus safety.

299
00:22:42.583 --> 00:22:48.471
Every message schema change must pass the registry's FULL compatibility check before it can be produced.

300
00:22:48.751 --> 00:22:50.329
R4, Backfills batched.

301
00:22:50.609 --> 00:22:56.177
No unbounded UPDATE or DELETE on a table over 100k rows; batch and commit.

302
00:22:56.457 --> 00:22:58.889
R5, Reversible until contract.

303
00:22:59.169 --> 00:23:06.657
Dual-write continues until the read-switch has been stable in production for one release; only then may the old shape be dropped.

304
00:23:08.007 --> 00:23:09.415
Decisions in detail.

305
00:23:09.695 --> 00:23:13.087
Online DDL only (ADR-140).

306
00:23:13.367 --> 00:23:16.866
Migrations run with SET locktimeout='3s'.

307
00:23:17.146 --> 00:23:22.799
Allowed: nullable or constant-default ADD COLUMN, CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, ADD CONSTRAINT...

308
00:23:23.079 --> 00:23:24.701
NOT VALID then VALIDATE.

309
00:23:24.981 --> 00:23:34.517
Forbidden without a maintenance window: volatile-default ADD COLUMN, in-place ALTER TYPE, naive SET NOT NULL, plain CREATE INDEX on large tables.

310
00:23:34.797 --> 00:23:36.525
(Rationale measured in L1.).

311
00:23:36.805 --> 00:23:40.901
Expand or contract for columns (ADR-141).

312
00:23:41.181 --> 00:23:45.725
The six phases (§2.4), each a separate deployable step.

313
00:23:46.005 --> 00:23:50.143
Rename and retype are always expand or contract, never in place.

314
00:23:50.423 --> 00:23:51.277
(L2.).

315
00:23:52.627 --> 00:23:55.613
Batched backfills (ADR-142).

316
00:23:55.893 --> 00:24:02.080
Key-range batches, commit per batch, optional throttle, driven off the PK or index, never OFFSET.

317
00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:03.256
(L4.).

318
00:24:03.536 --> 00:24:07.291
Bus under FULL compatibility (ADR-143).

319
00:24:07.571 --> 00:24:11.773
Protobuf, registry set to FULL, retired field numbers reserved.

320
00:24:12.053 --> 00:24:15.829
CI runs the compatibility check on every schema PR.

321
00:24:16.109 --> 00:24:17.027
(L3.).

322
00:24:17.307 --> 00:24:20.955
API additive-first (ADR-144).

323
00:24:21.235 --> 00:24:29.853
New or vN only for breaks; run versions in parallel; Deprecation or Sunset headers and caller telemetry before retiring.

324
00:24:30.133 --> 00:24:33.013
Store-to-store (ADR-145).

325
00:24:33.293 --> 00:24:41.955
Dual-write (preferably via outbox or CDC), batched backfill, continuous reconciliation, flagged read-switch, delayed decommission.

326
00:24:43.305 --> 00:24:46.953
Forward-only migrations (ADR-146).

327
00:24:47.233 --> 00:24:52.694
Numbered, applied once, tracked; a rollback is a new forward migration, not a down-script.

328
00:24:52.974 --> 00:24:53.998
Consequences.

329
00:24:54.278 --> 00:25:00.955
Changes take more steps and more than one release to complete, and engineers must think in compatible increments.

330
00:25:01.235 --> 00:25:08.830
In return: no migration outages, safe rollbacks, and independently-deployable producers or consumers or clients.

331
00:25:09.110 --> 00:25:12.609
The one-ALTER habit is explicitly traded away for safety.

332
